                        "entry_id": "246f0206-e684-357b-a578-932da4b390f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A conical, grooved pulley in early clocks, antique watches, and possibly all non-electronic marine chronometers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6af1f442-63d7-4d52-9318-6890a4132578",
                                "sense_id": "202e1ffe-01a0-34c6-a313-704926bd4456",
                                "text": "To day when we attended the winding up of the watches the fusee of Mr Arnolds would not turn round and after several unsuccessfull tryals we were obliged to let it go down […] ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fc510d03-da3f-3410-a5a9-48775042ee80",
                        "entry_id": "246f0206-e684-357b-a578-932da4b390f6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A large friction match."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd90a767-e0c0-4fd7-a183-f0c10aeb4858",
                                "sense_id": "fc510d03-da3f-3410-a5a9-48775042ee80",
                                "text": "A comfortable hammock on a warm afternoon would appeal to his indolent tastes, and then, when he was getting drowsy, a lighted fusee thrown into the nest would bring the wasps out in an indignant mass, and they would soon find a ‘home away from home’ on Waldo's fat body."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
